course: dictionary
lesson: 11278
title: Wristband: a band worn on the wrist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wristband is a band worn around the wrist. You can see the parts inside the word: wrist, the joint between your hand and arm, and band, a strip. Put them together and you get a strip worn on the wrist.
explain: The sentences show what a wristband can do. «Before you go in, agree a meeting point with your adult, and wear a wristband with their phone number so staff can call them.» Here the wristband carries information. Ask: what would fit in this sentence? The clues say a phone number is written on it, so wristband means a band that carries information.
explain: «He stays calm, goes to a steward in a bright jacket and shows his wristband.» Shows his wristband tells you the wristband is something a person can show to staff as proof. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: a band on the wrist that proves something still makes sense.
fact: A wristband is a band worn around the wrist.
fact: A wristband can be made of cloth, plastic, rubber or paper.
fact: A wristband can soak up sweat, show you have paid for entry, show support for a cause, or carry information.
fact: A «medical alert wristband» can show a medical problem, such as an allergy to peanuts.
fact: A wristband can also mean the strap of a watch or a smart device.
exercise: «He stays calm, goes to a steward in a bright jacket and shows his wristband.» What is the wristband most likely to be in this sentence? | A sweaty band for the tennis court | A phone number for staff | A type of bright jacket | *A band on the wrist that shows he is allowed in
exercise: «A wristband with a parent's phone number lets staff call your parent if you get lost.» What is the wristband mainly for here? | To soak up sweat in a race | *To carry information so staff can help | To tell the time | To make the wrist look nice
exercise: Tennis players wear sweatbands on their wrists. What is a sweatband closest to? | A ticket for a match | *A wristband worn to soak up sweat | A pair of trainers | A helmet
test: Which phrase means a wristband that shows a child has an allergy? | *medical alert wristband | fitness wristband | charity wristband | sunhat
test: What does wristband mean in «My new watch has a rubber wristband»? | A paper ticket for a festival | A band worn to show support for a cause | A bandage for a broken arm | *The strap of the watch
exam: Why might a child wear a wristband with a parent's phone number at a theme park? | To keep the sun off the wrist only | To tell the time at the park | *So staff can call a parent if the child gets lost | To show they like tennis
